                "text": "Add 1 to obtain a common multiple of 1 through 9; their LCM is 2520.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the required integer be $n$. Each remainder is one less than its divisor, so $n+1$ is divisible by every integer from 1 to 9. Using the greatest required power of each prime,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{LCM}(1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9)&=2^3\\times3^2\\times5\\times7\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9)&=2520.\\end{align*}$$\nThe smallest possible positive value of $n+1$ is therefore 2520.\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=2520-1\\\\n&=2519.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
